(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The limited C API's remainder (queue 268; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 268\"): the functions of queue 262's"] [4 1 "// list of natives not provided (`.tmp/q262/missing.txt`) that the world's _testlimitedcapi reaches and pyi's objects"] [5 1 "// answer directly: dicts, sets, lists, tuples, ints, floats, complex numbers, bytes, bytearrays, the number, mapping"] [6 1 "// and sequence protocols, str's core, weak references, imports' module table, PyMem. Each follows its CPython 3.14.10"] [7 1 "// definition (Objects/dictobject.c, setobject.c, listobject.c, tupleobject.c, longobject.c, floatobject.c,"] [8 1 "// complexobject.c, bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c, abstract.c, unicodeobject.c, weakrefobject.c, Python/import.c,"] [9 1 "// Objects/obmalloc.c): the type checks and their messages, the operation through pyi's own (its type's method or"] [10 1 "// protocol, as CPython's calls the type's slot). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [24 1 "// callMeth calls o's method name with args."] [33 1 "// each calls f on each item of iter(o) until it returns an error (Iterate's)."] [41 1 "// callBuiltin calls builtins.name with args."] [50 1 "// opArgs are a native's object arguments, nil for NULL; err when one is NULL (null_error)."] [70 1 "// bigOf is o as an int (its __index__), CPython's _PyNumber_Index."] [82 1 "// asUnsigned is PyLong_AsUnsignedLong's family: o an int (no __index__), in [0, 2**bits)."] [101 1 "// asSignedBits is PyLong_AsInt32's family: o's __index__ in the signed range of bits."] [113 1 "// unsignedIndex is PyLong_AsUInt32's family: o's __index__ in [0, 2**bits)."] [130 1 "// storeInt writes the int v of size bytes at p (an output argument), when p is not NULL."] [147 2 "// ---- dicts (Objects/dictobject.c) ----"] [150 70 "// PyDict_Check: a subclass's instance too"] [188 34 "// _PyErr_SetKeyError"] [212 2 "// PyDict_GetItem and GetItemString: borrowed, errors suppressed; an error but KeyError (an unhashable key, a key that"] [213 2 "// does not decode) reported as unraisable (dictobject.c's dict_getitem, PyErr_FormatUnraisable)"] [238 21 "// _PyObject_HashFast's error, not the lookup's"] [304 2 "// PyDict_Next(d, Py_ssize_t *pos, PyObject **key, PyObject **value): borrowed references"] [349 2 "// ---- sets (Objects/setobject.c) ----"] [375 3 "// set_contains_key: the key hashed as is (set's `in` retries an unhashable set as a frozenset; PySet_Contains not)"] [401 4 "// a brand new frozenset (C holds its only reference: PyFrozenSet_New's) is filled in place"] [409 4 "// _PyErr_BadInternalCall(__FILE__, __LINE__) of Objects/setobject.c's PySet_Add (a frozenset too: pyi's are"] [410 4 "// never brand new to C)"] [437 2 "// ---- lists and tuples (Objects/listobject.c, tupleobject.c) ----"] [535 2 "// ---- ints (Objects/longobject.c) ----"] [565 2 "// PyLong_FromVoidPtr: a pointer that is an object's handle keeps the handle (a reference the process keeps), so that"] [566 2 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr gives the same object back while Python holds it (a handle C no longer references is released)"] [576 3 "// PyLong_FromString reads ASCII digits only (int() of a str takes the Unicode decimal digits, which"] [577 3 "// _PyUnicode_TransformDecimalAndSpaceToASCII gives it): a byte past 0x7f is long_from_string_base's invalid"] [578 3 "// literal, with the string decoded as UTF-8 (Objects/longobject.c)"] [606 2 "// longobject.c's messages, as they are"] [619 2 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr: an int (no __index__: \"an integer is required\") as a pointer; NULL on an error"] [653 2 "// PyLong_AsInt32 (o, int32_t *out) and the family: 0, or -1 with an error"] [658 24 "// *value left as it was"] [674 2 "// ---- floats and complex numbers ----"] [680 3 "// a str or a buffer only (Objects/floatobject.c; queue 270): float() also takes numbers"] [699 3 "// a new sys.float_info (floatobject.c's PyFloat_GetInfo makes one each call)"] [709 2 "// PyComplex_RealAsDouble and ImagAsDouble: capi_tail.go (asCComplex)"] [710 2 "// ---- the number protocol (Objects/abstract.c) ----"] [740 2 "// ---- the mapping and sequence protocols ----"] [775 2 "// the string-keyed forms (Objects/abstract.c): a NULL object or key is null_error's SystemError, the key decoded as"] [776 2 "// PyUnicode_FromString decodes it (its UnicodeDecodeError propagates)"] [810 2 "// PyMapping_HasKey and the rest: PyMapping_GetOptionalItem's lookup, a KeyError alone meaning absent (an IndexError"] [811 2 "// propagates); the forms without WithError report any error as unraisable, by their own message, and give 0"] [968 2 "// ---- bytes and bytearrays (Objects/bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c) ----"] [976 2 "// PyBytes_Repr(o, smartquotes) (Objects/bytesobject.c): double quotes only when smartquotes and the bytes hold a"] [977 2 "// single quote and no double quote; else single quotes, a single quote escaped"] [1021 47 "// the mirror's ob_sval (queue 269)"] [1029 2 "// PyBytes_Concat and PyBytes_ConcatAndDel (Objects/bytesobject.c): *pv NULL does nothing, w NULL clears *pv (no"] [1030 2 "// error), else *pv becomes bytes_concat's new bytes of the two buffers (a bytes-like object each, a C-contiguous"] [1031 2 "// one: anything else \"can't concat W to V\"), NULL on an error"] [1100 2 "// PyByteArray_Concat (Objects/bytearrayobject.c): a new bytearray of the two buffers (PyBUF_SIMPLE: a C-contiguous"] [1101 2 "// bytes-like object each, else \"can't concat B to A\")"] [1139 2 "// ---- str's core (Objects/unicodeobject.c) ----"] [1153 2 "// ensureStr is unicodeobject.c's ensure_unicode: an argument that is no str a TypeError \"must be str, not T\""] [1165 2 "// PyUnicode_GetLength and PyUnicode_ReadChar: an object that is no str is PyErr_BadArgument's TypeError; ReadChar's"] [1166 2 "// error is (Py_UCS4)-1, the 32-bit all-ones"] [1200 56 "// a subclass's instance: a new exact str (_PyUnicode_Copy)"] [1228 2 "// the str methods' natives: each str argument through ensure_unicode"] [1307 2 "// PyUnicode_Contains, Count, Find, FindChar and Tailmatch over the code points (their slices adjusted as"] [1308 2 "// ADJUST_INDICES does; a lone surrogate is a code point of its own)"] [1432 2 "// PyUnicode_EqualToUTF8 and EqualToUTF8AndSize: the str's strict UTF-8 (a surrogate never equal) against the size"] [1433 2 "// bytes, compared only when the sizes agree (no byte read past the str's own length)"] [1483 2 "// PyUnicode_AsXXXString and PyUnicode_AsEncodedString: an object that is no str is PyErr_BadArgument's TypeError"] [1515 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeXXX(const char *s, Py_ssize_t size, const char *errors)"] [1557 33 "// PyObject_GetBuffer(PyBUF_SIMPLE)"] [1563 2 "// ---- weak references (Objects/weakrefobject.c) ----"] [1587 2 "// ---- the module table (Python/import.c) ----"] [1616 2 "// PYC_MAGIC_NUMBER_TOKEN (Include/internal/pycore_magic_number.h: 3627, CPython 3.14's) as import.c gives it"] [1617 2 "// PyImport_GetMagicNumber (Python/import.c): the magic number of the interpreter's own importlib, its"] [1618 2 "// _bootstrap_external.MAGIC_NUMBER's four bytes as a little-endian long (pyi's, as importlib.util.MAGIC_NUMBER)"] [1650 2 "// PyImport_ImportModuleLevelObject (Python/import.c): name NULL is ValueError \"Empty module name\", a level < 0"] [1651 2 "// ValueError, a relative import's globals that are no dict TypeError \"globals must be a dict\" (resolve_name), then"] [1652 2 "// builtins.__import__'s own checks"] [1701 24 "// any hashable name (PyModule_NewObject keeps it as __name__)"] [1709 31 "// borrowed: sys.modules holds it"] [1722 2 "// ---- types (Objects/typeobject.c): every pyi type is ready; the cache is pyi's own"] [1727 3 "// a type object of C's memory (queue 269): a static PyTypeObject, or one C filled after type's tp_alloc"] [1734 2 "// ---- the codecs' stateful decoders (Objects/unicodeobject.c over _codecs' functions)"] [1736 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeUTF16(s, size, errors, int *byteorder) and its Stateful (..., Py_ssize_t *consumed)"] [1781 3 "// PyUnicode_DecodeUTF8Stateful(s, size, errors, Py_ssize_t *consumed)"] [1814 2 "// PyUnicode_Translate is _PyUnicode_TranslateCharmap: a code point the mapping lacks (LookupError) is kept, one it"] [1815 2 "// maps to None is undefined, given to the errors handler (str.translate deletes it)"] [1823 33 "// _PyUnicode_TranslateCharmap's PyErr_BadArgument"] [1831 2 "// ---- files (Objects/fileobject.c) ----"] [1837 3 "// a bool warns (Objects/fileobject.c, 3.14; py-eval-1122: test_file's test_pyobject_asfiledescriptor)"] [1882 17 "// PyFile_WriteObject of NULL writes \"<NULL>\" (py-eval-1122: it was a Go panic)"] [1884 29 "// Py_PRINT_RAW"] [1955 2 "// ---- memory (Objects/obmalloc.c) ----"] [1956 2 "// PyMem_Malloc, Calloc, Realloc and Free: capi_tail.go (the allocator domains)"] [1957 2 "// the inline accessors of the old limited versions, functions since 3.14's (Include/object.h)"] [1972 1 "// appendStr is PyUnicode_Append (PyObject **pleft, PyObject *right) and AppendAndDel."] [2005 1 "// cmpRunes is PyUnicode_Compare's order: by code point."] [2025 1 "// builtinMethod is a built-in type's method by name (list.sort)."] [2031 1 "// getargsKeywords is PyArg_ParseTupleAndKeywords (Python/getargs.c, vgetargskeywords): the positional arguments and the"] [2032 1 "// keywords of kwargs (nil: none) converted by format into the pointers, the parameters named by kwlist (a char *[] in"] [2033 1 "// the world, NULL-terminated; empty names are positional-only)."] [2119 5 "// PyDict_GetItemStringRef: the name decoded strictly (an invalid one is its UnicodeDecodeError; queue 270)"] [2152 63 "// skipitem leaves the format at the unit"] [2189 4 "// new_kwtuple: the keyword-capable names decoded strictly (an invalid one is its UnicodeDecodeError)"] [2198 27 "// (without _Py_CalculateSuggestions' \"Did you mean\")"] [2206 3 "// every extra keyword matched a name (a str subclass whose hash is not its text's: queue 270)"] [2216 1 "// replaceUTF8 is a C string as PyErr_Format